      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A great analogy is listening to a complex orchestra. Time-domain analysis is like hearing the entire music as one continuous sound wave. The Fourier Transform is like having a perfect score and knowing exactly how many violins, flutes, and timpani are playing, and precisely how loudly each is playing at any moment. The \"hidden\" part is the underlying periodic structure; your ear blends it, but the math separates it into its constituent pure tones.",
